[1m[38;5;231mWhat's the default for a field that isn't explicitly classified?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mDeny by default (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOnly explicitly-allowlisted keys reach a record, plus a name-based scrubber as a backstop. Mistakes cost a missing
[39m     [38;5;246mfield, never a leaked credential.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Allow by default (denylist)
     [38;5;246mEverything is logged except keys matching a known-sensitive name list. Lower friction; leaks anything nobody [39m
     [38;5;246mthought to add to the list.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Messages only, no payloads
     [38;5;246mLog strings only, never structured context. Nothing can leak, but debugging value drops sharply.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
